LRC integer-programming mode lens (codex-2026-05-31 S420)
The calculation treats natural numbers as odd-core x+2 chains with vertical x*2 doublings, then builds exact LRC row/column ledgers.

========================================================================================
SPEED COLUMNS AS ODD-CORE / DOUBLING MODES
========================================================================================
A speed column is written v=2^h*odd_core.  h is the vertical x*2 height; odd_core moves horizontally by x+2.
label                  n  dyadic h-counts        odd-core counts
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
n14 initial            14  0:7 1:3 2:2 3:1        1:4 3:3 5:2 7:1 9:1 11:1 13:1
n14 drop13 add14       14  0:6 1:4 2:2 3:1        1:4 3:3 5:2 7:2 9:1 11:1
n14 drop13 add182      14  0:6 1:4 2:2 3:1        1:4 3:3 5:2 7:1 9:1 11:1 91:1
n14 S380 gate ladder   14  0:1 1:7 2:2 3:2 4:1    1:1 7:4 21:2 35:2 49:1 63:1 77:1 91:1
n16 initial            16  0:8 1:4 2:2 3:1        1:4 3:3 5:2 7:2 9:1 11:1 13:1 15:1
n16 drop15 add16       16  0:7 1:4 2:2 3:1 4:1    1:5 3:3 5:2 7:2 9:1 11:1 13:1
n16 best 8-ladder      16  0:1 3:8 4:3 5:2 6:1    1:5 3:3 5:2 7:1 9:1 11:1 13:1 15:1

========================================================================================
SMALL-DENOMINATOR IP INVOICES
========================================================================================
Rows are m=2..n.  A speed column pays row m exactly when m divides it. Missing rows give immediate THM-366 witnesses.
label                  missing rows       fragile one-payer rows
